Package: PredictProR
Type: Package
Title: Genomic and Multi-Omics Prediction Workflows
Version: 0.20.188
Author: Sikiru Atanda
Maintainer: PredictProR maintainer <sikiru.atanda@ndsu.edu>
Description: Genomic and multi-omics prediction for diploid and polyploid
    crops through one workflow function. Covers genotype quality control,
    recoding and imputation (native k-nearest-neighbour and mean imputation,
    and 'Beagle' for diploid data), conversion of 'VCF', 'HapMap' and CSV/TXT
    genotype files, ploidy-aware genomic relationship matrices and kernels,
    multi-omics layers and kernels, and predictor (feature) selection. Models
    include Bayesian marker and kernel regression ('BGLR'), 'ASReml-R' mixed
    models, Gaussian process models, classical machine learning and deep
    learning (through 'Python'). Supports single- and multi-environment
    trials, single- and multi-trait analysis, hybrid prediction with general
    and specific combining ability, and binary, ordinal and multiclass traits,
    with cross-validation schemes (including CV0, CV1 and CV2), variance
    components, prediction uncertainty and reliability, and parallel
    execution.
